Fix PHP 8.4 implicit-nullable-parameter deprecation

ElasticsearchIndexBase::dispatchOperationErrorEvent() declares
$request_wrapper as implicitly nullable (typed param with a NULL
default and no explicit ?-prefix), which PHP 8.4 deprecates. Since
Drupal's development environment prints deprecation notices directly
into the response body, this corrupts every REST endpoint that calls
this method on error, breaking the JSON content type contract (e.g.
/autocomplete, /search/games).

--- a/src/Plugin/ElasticsearchIndexBase.php
+++ b/src/Plugin/ElasticsearchIndexBase.php
@@ -192,6 +192,6 @@
    *
    * @return \Drupal\elasticsearch_helper\Event\ElasticsearchOperationErrorEvent
    */
-  protected function dispatchOperationErrorEvent(\Throwable $error, $operation, ElasticsearchRequestWrapperInterface $request_wrapper = NULL, $object = NULL, $metadata = []) {
+  protected function dispatchOperationErrorEvent(\Throwable $error, $operation, ?ElasticsearchRequestWrapperInterface $request_wrapper = NULL, $object = NULL, $metadata = []) {
     $event = new ElasticsearchOperationErrorEvent($error, $operation, $this, $request_wrapper, $object, $metadata);
     $this->getEventDispatcher()->dispatch($event, ElasticsearchEvents::OPERATION_ERROR);
